.SH DIAGNOSTICS
As in TinyGL, invalid or unsupported operations are fatal.
There is no recoverable GL error queue.
.SH BUGS
This is an experimental subset, not a conformant OpenGL implementation.
There is no stencil, fog, multisampling, programmable shader API or selection.
Unsupported operations are rejected; functions absent from the header are
not provided. Lighting retains TinyGL's approximations.
.PP
Only one current context per process is supported; calls are not thread-safe.
There is no GLX, EGL, GLUT, surface sharing or direct presentation.
Readback and libdraw composition still copy pixels through CPU memory.
The client has been tested on amd64 with QEMU VirGL and inherits the
privileges and failure behavior described in
.IR gpu (3).
